</div>
</div>
<div class="hidden space-y-2.5" id="crownDiceStep">
<p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700" id="crownDicePromptText">Enter desired dice values (comma-separated for 2 dice, e.g. 6,6 or 6,2):</p>
<input class="w-full bg-white border-2 border-amber-400 rounded-xl px-3 py-2 text-sm font-black text-slate-900 font-mono" id="crownDiceValuesInput" placeholder="e.g. 6,6 or 5" type="text"/>
<button class="w-full py-2.5 px-4 rounded-xl font-black text-xs emerald-play-btn" id="applyComingDiceBtn" type="button">✅ Set Coming Roll</button>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="hidden fixed inset-0 z-50 bg-slate-900/75 backdrop-blur-sm flex items-center justify-center p-3 sm:p-4" id="multiMouseModal">
<div class="royal-card rounded-3xl p-4 sm:p-5 max-w-2xl w-full max-h-[90dvh] overflow-y-auto border-2 border-indigo-500 shadow-2xl space-y-3.5">
<div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-indigo-200 pb-2.5">
<div>
<h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black text-slate-900">🖱️ Multi-Mouse Hardware Setup &amp; Calibration (2–4 Mice)</h3>
<p class="text-[11px] text-slate-600">Lock each physical mouse (<code>event.pointerId</code>) to a specific player seat so nobody can roll or touch another player's beads.</p>
</div>
<button class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-slate-100 hover:bg-slate-200 text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 flex-shrink-0" id="closeMultiMouseModalBtn" type="button">✕</button>
</div>
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 p-3 rounded-2xl bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-300">
<label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs sm:text-sm font-black text-indigo-950 cursor-pointer">
<input class="w-4 h-4 accent-indigo-600 rounded" id="modalMultiMouseEnableChk" type="checkbox"/>
<span>Enable Multi-Mouse Per-Player Lock</span>
</label>
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
<button class="mm-preset-btn px-2.5 py-1 rounded-xl bg-white hover:bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-900 border border-indigo-300 text-[11px] font-extrabold" data-count="2" type="button">2 Mice (1v1)</button>
<button class="mm-preset-btn px-2.5 py-1 rounded-xl bg-white hover:bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-900 border border-indigo-300 text-[11px] font-extrabold" data-count="3" type="button">3 Mice (3P)</button>
<button class="mm-preset-btn px-2.5 py-1 rounded-xl bg-white hover:bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-900 border border-indigo-300 text-[11px] font-extrabold" data-count="4" type="button">4 Mice (4P)</button>
<button class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-xl bg-rose-100 hover:bg-rose-200 text-rose-800 border border-rose-300 text-[11px] font-bold" id="clearAllMiceBtn" type="button">🗑️ Reset IDs</button>
</div>
</div>
<div class="p-3 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900 text-white border border-amber-400/60 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
<div class="text-xs font-bold text-amber-300" id="mmWizardPromptText">
        👆 Click any player's target box below using that player's physical mouse to bind its Hardware Pointer ID!
      </div>
<button class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-xl gold-gradient-btn text-xs font-black" id="startMmWizardBtn" type="button">
        ▶️ Step-by-Step Wizard
      </button>
</div>
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2.5" id="mmSeatCalibrationGrid"></div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50/70 p-3.5 space-y-2.5 text-xs text-slate-800">
<div class="font-black text-sm text-amber-950">📖 Complete Factual Step-by-Step Setup Guide (Windows &amp; Linux)</div>
<p class="text-[11px] text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        By default, Windows and macOS merge all plugged-in mice into a single cursor (`pointerId: 1`). To make your browser receive a separate `event.pointerId` for each physical mouse on a single laptop, follow these exact steps:
      </p>
<div class="space-y-1.5 bg-white p-3 rounded-xl border border-amber-200">
<div class="font-black text-indigo-900">🪟 Method A: Windows (2, 3, or 4 Mice)</div>
<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-1 text-[11px] text-slate-700">
<li>Plug in <b>2, 3, or 4 USB/Wireless mice</b> into your Windows laptop.</li>
<li>Install and launch a multi-cursor driver utility such as <b>TeamPlayer4</b> (by Dicolab/IdeaCom) or <b>MouseMux</b>.</li>
<li>Enable <b>Independent Native Pointer / Multi-Pointer Injection</b> in the driver settings so each physical mouse gets its own colored cursor and unique Windows Pointer ID.</li>
<li>Click <b>"2 Mice"</b>, <b>"3 Mice"</b>, or <b>"4 Mice"</b> above, then have each player click their respective colored box above with their own mouse.</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="space-y-1.5 bg-white p-3 rounded-xl border border-amber-200">
<div class="font-black text-emerald-900">🐧 Method B: Linux (Built-in Native XInput — No Extra Software Needed!)</div>
<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-1 text-[11px] text-slate-700">
<li>Plug in your extra mice and open a terminal. Run <code>xinput list</code> to see each mouse's device ID (e.g., <code>id=12</code>, <code>id=13</code>).</li>
<li>Create an independent master cursor for each additional player:<br/>
<code class="bg-slate-900 text-emerald-300 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[10px]">xinput create-master Player2</code> (and <code>Player3</code>, <code>Player4</code>)</li>
<li>Run <code>xinput list</code> again to find the new Master Pointer ID (e.g., <code>Player2 pointer [id=18]</code>).</li>
<li>Attach the physical mouse to its new master cursor:<br/>
<code class="bg-slate-900 text-emerald-300 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[10px]">xinput reattach 12 18</code></li>
<li>Now open this game in Chrome/Edge/Firefox and click each player's calibration box above!</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="space-y-1 bg-white p-3 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 text-[11px] text-slate-700">
<div class="font-black text-rose-900">🛡️ How Enforcement Works During Match:</div>
<p>• When it is <b>Red's turn</b>, only Red's calibrated mouse (`pointerId`) can click <b>🎲 Roll Dice</b>, filter dice, or drag/tap Red's beads on the board.</p>
<p>• If Green, Yellow, or Blue tries to click the dice or touch any bead during Red's turn, their hardware `pointerId` is rejected with a warning banner.</p>
<p>• If a player's seat is left uncalibrated (`Unassigned`), any mouse is allowed for that seat as a safe fallback so you never get stuck.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="flex justify-end gap-2 pt-1">
<button class="px-5 py-2 rounded-xl font-black text-xs emerald-play-btn" id="doneMultiMouseModalBtn" type="button">✅ Done &amp; Save</button>
</div>
</div>
</div>
